Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Fix bd CLI integration - remove non-existent --no-db flag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Critical fix for bd CLI compatibility:

Changes to beads.py:
- Removed --no-db flag (doesn't exist in bd CLI)
- Changed to use standard bd commands with SQLite database
- Updated get_status() to use 'bd stats' command
- Updated get_all_tasks() to use 'bd list --json'
- Status mapping: open/in_progress/closed

Changes to docs/DESIGN.md:
- Updated Phase 1 description to reflect SQLite usage
- Removed incorrect --no-db reference

Why this matters:
- The --no-db flag was never implemented in bd CLI
- bd uses SQLite for transactional integrity
- JSONL is synced automatically via --no-auto-flush flag
- Database provides proper concurrency control for multi-agent

Tested and verified working:
✅ bd stats parses correctly
✅ bd ready returns ready tasks
✅ bd list --json returns full task details
✅ bd update works for status and assignee
✅ Dashboard loads with correct counts
✅ Full claim/complete workflow functional
